{"h":3406,"w":2400,"lines":[{"h":0.01453488361674482,"y":0.03924418608314173,"t":"Introduction","x":0.82886597715679444,"w":0.1237113444010417,"c":1},{"x":0.051546392174427351,"h":0.01453488361674482,"t":"ACADEMIC TEST FORMAT","w":0.36907216389973957,"y":0.088662790745637876,"c":1},{"t":"Listening","x":0.053165534188370861,"h":0.017063904704588406,"c":1,"w":0.11025436401367186,"y":0.12535691432564688},{"w":0.81030929565429699,"h":0.017441861012089666,"y":0.1511627904200934,"c":1,"t":"This test consists of four sections, each with ten questions. The first two sections are","x":0.053608238666728973},{"c":1,"x":0.051546405318339247,"t":"concerned with social needs. The first section is a conversation between two speakers and","w":0.87216491699218768,"y":0.16999412800578961,"h":0.016147974163241319},{"y":0.18895348853874727,"c":1,"h":0.015988371754420583,"w":0.8453608194986979,"t":"the second section is a monologue. The final two sections are concerned with situations","x":0.051546394295848001},{"c":1,"w":0.88453613281249999,"t":"related to educational or training contexts. The third section is a conversation between up to","h":0.015988371754420583,"x":0.049484510816262928,"y":0.20784883737657467},{"y":0.22516208689266537,"x":0.049389032117464919,"h":0.017736972533319628,"c":1,"t":"four people and the fourth section is a monologue.","w":0.4867994181315104},{"x":0.074226799017626494,"t":"A variety of question types is used, including: multiple choice, matching, plan\/map\/","y":0.24418604623537254,"w":0.79381444295247394,"c":1,"h":0.017441861012089777},{"h":0.017458076835448644,"w":0.89278350830078113,"c":1,"y":0.26306517924989525,"x":0.051546390072696131,"t":"diagram labelling, form completion, note completion, table completion, flow-chart completion,"},{"x":0.049484548592796787,"w":0.65773193359374993,"c":1,"h":0.017615971814445075,"y":0.28185554887084296,"t":"summary completion, sentence completion, short-answer questions."},{"w":0.82680414835611971,"h":0.017441861012089666,"c":1,"t":"Candidates hear the recording once only and answer the questions as they listen. Ten","x":0.072164936025994567,"y":0.29941860437542256},{"h":0.016888104952298755,"w":0.88461263020833325,"y":0.31743151567702133,"t":"minutes are allowed at the end for candidates to transfer their answers to the answer sheet.","c":1,"x":0.049455078935087708},{"w":0.097876001993815076,"h":0.017252791578883042,"c":1,"y":0.34939549597820785,"t":"Reading","x":0.051190157191201152},{"h":0.016147974163241319,"c":1,"x":0.051546386138594753,"y":0.37639459761026717,"t":"This test consists of three sections with 40 questions. There are three texts, which are","w":0.82474227905273445},{"c":1,"y":0.39534883693350231,"x":0.049484538069152678,"w":0.87628865559895841,"h":0.017452102791052027,"t":"taken from journals, books, magazines and newspapers. The texts are on topics of general"},{"x":0.047422683966817182,"h":0.017441861012089666,"t":"interest. At least one text contains detailed logical argument.","y":0.41279069739594854,"c":1,"w":0.58350514729817715},{"c":1,"y":0.4315913093598549,"t":"A variety of question types is used, including: multiple choice, identifying information","w":0.81030929565429688,"h":0.017615971814445075,"x":0.072164939701697031},{"t":"(True\/False\/Not Given), identifying the writer's views\/claims (Yes\/No\/Not Given), matching","h":0.01889534914976565,"c":1,"w":0.86597930908203113,"x":0.047422719170324493,"y":0.44912790658427415},{"y":0.46799765119864078,"h":0.017467464619500439,"t":"information, matching headings, matching features, matching sentence endings, sentence","c":1,"x":0.04742271557017811,"w":0.86804117838541672},{"y":0.48678802098798302,"h":0.017615971814445075,"c":1,"x":0.049484517737476398,"w":0.88247426350911451,"t":"completion, summary completion, note completion, table completion, flow-chart completion,"},{"h":0.017441861012089777,"c":1,"x":0.049484529414754709,"t":"diagram label completion, short-answer questions.","y":0.50581395321079103,"w":0.48659795125325517},{"x":0.048760591045051434,"w":0.086175231933593749,"h":0.018326449660224453,"y":0.53593273178397161,"t":"Writing","c":1},{"h":0.015988371754420694,"x":0.049484528103634864,"w":0.86391754150390621,"t":"This test consists of two tasks. It is suggested that candidates spend about 20 minutes on","c":1,"y":0.56250000016718082},{"x":0.049484548562433679,"w":0.85773193359375011,"h":0.017615971814445075,"y":0.58132706984850446,"t":"Task 1, which requires them to write at least 150 words, and 40 minutes on Task 2, which","c":1},{"t":"requires them to write at least 250 words. Task 2 contributes twice as much as Task 1 to the","y":0.5985810138589156,"w":0.88256306966145837,"h":0.017101591359988011,"c":1,"x":0.047379539897231857},{"c":1,"t":"Writing score.","w":0.13478009541829428,"y":0.6185764302232426,"x":0.049058521920021789,"h":0.015605505396181663},{"c":1,"x":0.072164944155659327,"t":"Task 1 requires candidates to look at a diagram or some data (graph, table or chart) and","w":0.84742268880208338,"y":0.63652378136464727,"h":0.016147974163241319},{"t":"to present the information in their own words. They are assessed on their ability to organise,","x":0.045284943394682954,"w":0.88884816487630214,"h":0.021695952939063234,"c":1,"y":0.65130231644322367},{"t":"present and possibly compare data, describe the stages of a process, describe an object or","y":0.6720002888421035,"x":0.047354432728930362,"w":0.88261973063151056,"h":0.020886046565846028,"c":1},{"x":0.047279843774770472,"y":0.69046712773522467,"w":0.38168299357096358,"h":0.019180382971055288,"c":1,"t":"event, or explain how something works."},{"t":"In Task 2, candidates are presented with a point of view, argument or problem. They are","x":0.068041225993769383,"w":0.84948455810546886,"c":1,"y":0.71075581367763185,"h":0.017441861012089777},{"y":0.72775155796251612,"t":"assessed on their ability to present a solution to the problem, present and justify an opinion,","w":0.88466410319010413,"h":0.019369048086671503,"x":0.047366157952340206,"c":1},{"w":0.85567006429036452,"h":0.017441859892096456,"y":0.74709302352336537,"t":"compare and contrast evidence and opinions, evaluate and challenge ideas, evidence or","x":0.045360844679111667,"c":1},{"t":"arguments.","w":0.11144255320231121,"h":0.014928989108002222,"c":1,"x":0.047371507480275535,"y":0.76724480762418878},{"c":1,"t":"Candidates are also assessed on their ability to write in an appropriate style.","w":0.73608245849609377,"y":0.78479154452631439,"x":0.072164956201662273,"h":0.01614797416324143},{"y":0.81092190257480112,"h":0.017615971814445075,"w":0.81855672200520835,"t":"More information on assessing the Writing test, including Writing Assessment Criteria","x":0.047422669820809539,"c":1},{"w":0.48865976969401032,"c":1,"t":"(public version), is available on the IELTS website.","x":0.045360836714265863,"h":0.017441859892096456,"y":0.82848837237054251},{"c":1,"x":0.92577319574042349,"t":"5","y":0.94622093013930197,"w":0.014432989756266279,"h":0.01453488361674482},{"y":0.95433624955947682,"h":0.022583511809496359,"t":"leltsresources.org","x":0.35219444028158703,"c":1,"w":0.29146217346191411}]}